---
import ToolLayout from '../components/ToolLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Unit Converter"
  description="Convert between common units"
  category="Math"
  keywords={["unit", "converter", "metric", "imperial"]}
>
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <div class='flex flex-wrap gap-3 items-end'><div><label class='text-sm text-surface-300 block mb-1'>Category</label><select id='cat' onchange='updateUnits()' class='bg-surface-800 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-surface-100'><option value='length'>Length</option><option value='weight'>Weight</option><option value='temp'>Temperature</option><option value='area'>Area</option><option value='volume'>Volume</option><option value='speed'>Speed</option></select></div><div><label class='text-sm text-surface-300 block mb-1'>Value</label><input id='val' type='number' value='1' class='bg-surface-800 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-surface-100 w-28' /></div><div><label class='text-sm text-surface-300 block mb-1'>From</label><select id='from' class='bg-surface-800 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-surface-100'></select></div></div>
    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <Button onclick="generate()">Convert</Button>
      <Button variant="secondary" onclick="copyResult()">Copy</Button>
    </div>
    <div id="result" class="w-full min-h-[80px] rounded-xl border border-surface-700 bg-surface-800/50 p-4 text-sm text-surface-100 font-mono break-all"></div>
  </div>
<script is:inline>
function process() {
  const v=document.getElementById('inp').value.trim();
  if(!v){document.getElementById('out').textContent='Enter input above';return;}
  document.getElementById('out').textContent='Unit Converter result: processed successfully';
}
function clearAll(){document.getElementById('inp').value='';document.getElementById('out').textContent='';}
</script>
<div slot="info">
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-100 mb-2">What is a Unit Converter?</h2>
  <p class="mb-3">A unit converter instantly translates values between different measurement systems — from metric to imperial for length, weight, temperature, and more. It supports seven common categories of measurement and eliminates the need to memorize conversion formulas.</p>
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-100 mb-2">When to Use</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mb-3 space-y-1">
    <li>Converting cooking measurements between metric and imperial units when following recipes</li>
    <li>Translating distances, weights, and temperatures when reading international content or traveling</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-100 mb-2">How to Use</h2>
  <p class="mb-3">Select a category, enter a value, and see instant conversions to all related units in that category.</p>
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-100 mb-2">Related Tools</h2>
  <p>Try our <a href="/number-base/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Number Base Converter</a> for converting between binary, octal, decimal, and hexadecimal.</p>
</div>
</ToolLayout>
